eed the beast or fleece  the government the kingston's over the  years have been investigated  for tax fraud  child welfare fraud one of the more  common things that former members told  me  they would do and they were encouraged  to do by their leaders  is a mother would go in and claim that  she was a single mom  with seven kids to qualify  for different benefits when in fact she  could have been the third or fourth wife  of a husband  over the past few years members of the  kingston family  who ran a different company called  waushaki renewable energy  have pleaded guilty to dozens of charges  including fraud  money laundering and obstruction jacob  kingston from what i understand  actually had the idea to build  this biodiesel production  plant he recognized that there was a  huge opportunity  the federal government was really  pushing  renewable energy alternative fuels  and there were big tax credits you could  get  prior to jacob they had  sort of focused on businesses like pawn  shops  um or you know commercial property  that's kind of  shabbier jacob was taking them into the  big leagues where  you know he's standing courtside at  halftime at a  utah jazz game presenting a big check to  a charity  so this really was a matter of  moving from the shadows into  the public arena you could almost think  of like  the godfather or any sort of mafia movie  where  over time you know you want to go into  legitimate business you don't want to  live in the shadows anymore  after jacob kingston got his phd  in engineering he then set up  a plant in northern utah on his father's  ranch  what they did was produce biodiesel fuel  which  takes animal fat or used cooking oil  and through a chemical process converts  it into a type of fuel  that works in trucks and in  manufacturing facilities the pure  version of that fuel  is known as b100 and what  they then did was apply for  tax credits that are administered by  both the environmental protection agency  and the internal revenue service those  tax credits  were a dollar a gallon for the fuel that  they produced  that was b100 or what's called b99 a  slightly diluted version  and they also got credit for a renewable  identification number or a win rin  and that was a dollar a gallon as well  and those are sort of a unique  number that can be traded between  companies  washiki renewable energy a proud partner  of the tour of utah is leading the  intermountain west to a future where our  air is clear  clean and healthy it did start as a  legitimate business  kingston found that he could not compete  because of the limitations on his  location  and the difficulties in producing the  material so he began to cut corners and  cheat  the way other people in the industry did  as well  [Music]  in 2011 washiki had run into some  troubles  the biodiesel they were creating called  b99  was being rejected it wasn't pure enough  and so he was looking for someone  to buy it and so he had sent a salesman  out  to people who were involved in this  business who might buy it and that's how  he came across  lev durman and that was the beginning of  what initially was a really profitable  enterprise for both of them  lev durman who called himself the lion  was a man who you could say a self-made  immigrant who created an oil and gas  empire in southern california and  in his adult life he was constantly  under investigation and we talked  to one of his associates who said that  the first time he met lev  he was struck by a guy who was almost  like wearing a costume of a mobster  he's wearing blue alligator shoes a blue  alligator belt  you know he had an office in rodeo drive  and it was like hey let's  go down here for a meal  you know my chauffeur will take us  and you know it's like a block away but  hey if i can get into my  rolls royce and take you a block and the  restaurant shut down just for me  um that's gonna create this appearance  that  i am um i don't know like an organized  crime boss  and so he sort of carried himself that  way it's a question of how much of that  was just for appearance  and how much of that was real  [Music]  when they first met left durman flew his  private jet to utah to meet  jacob kingston and his wife sally german  then flew them to seattle  to meet a friend of his he wined them  and dined them  the kingstons had never been wined and  dined before  they'd never been on a private jet they  went to a seafood store  and lev derman bought  the entire contents of the seafood store  to bring home for the kingstons  over time jacob kingston  was dazzled by lev fast living lifestyle  they bought very expensive sports cars  like a 1.8 million dollar bugatti  for lev durman they bought waterfront  house in california  for leb german they bought a three  million dollar house  in utah for jacob kingston  they took trips together he started  dressing in a flashier way  started wearing cologne he started  cutting his hair differently  it really started to change him he got a  taste for the high life  and he wanted that and in pursuing that  he was sort of breaking an  unspoken order rule and that rule is to  not draw attention  if you start wearing flashy suits and  driving  fancy cars and having  a luxury suite at utah jazz games  being public with your company  sponsoring different things  you're gonna draw attention and so jacob  had a dilemma do we  keep operating the way my uncles  have run the family by staying in the  shadows  or do we go big do we try to make a lot  of money  and for whatever reason he chose the  latter  the epa did not enforce its standards  stringently  and what fraudsters soon learned  is that if they were able to produce  documentation that showed  that they had produced biodiesel fuel  that the government accepted that  documentation and they got  you know their credits eventually the  government got more sophisticated at  rooting out the fraudsters but there  were several years  particularly in the early years jacob  kingston and left durman  perpetrating their fraud that the  government was not  able to keep up with the fraudsters  so there was one particular fraud where  the kingstons and lev durman  used a supplier in florida  and houston who shipped b99  on a barge and senate to the east coast  of panama  and that generated phony paperwork and  then  they trucked it over to the west coast  of panama  and they put it on a different boat and  shipped it up to los  angeles where lev durman's company said  that he was  shipping it to utah for processing  at kingston biodiesel fuel plant the  washaki plant  i talked to a guy who worked for jacob  and he told me that they filled up an  entire rail car with water  as long as they had the documents to  show that they were moving what looked  like biodiesel  the inspections were so laxed to  basically like non-existent  but that was enough to fool the  government and cash in on these tax  credits  the largest and most dramatic example  were two checks combined totaled more  than 160 million dollars that was  ultimately their biggest payday  there were other claims that they put in  that were  disallowed as the government eventually  caught on  fully to their fraud jacob kingston and  his family were arrested  as they boarded a plane in salt lake  city  headed for turkey anything you'd like to  say  a lot of the initial questions that  prosecutors were starting to ask  kind of tipped their hand that this  wasn't going to just be  a case about washing renewable energy  this was going to be a case about the  order and all of their businesses  and this would put everything they had  built at risk  so in a way you know jacob took this big  gamble for the family you know let's go  big time  let's step out of the shadows let's make  a lot of money  and at the end he paid the ultimate  price  yeah that's right the kingston clan has  their fingers in all kinds of businesses  oil lubes grocery stores hardware stores  private investigator firms biodiesel and  that biodiesel  allegedly helped pay for that four  million dollar mansion in sandy where  one of those warrants was served today  the prosecutors were helped at trial by  the cooperation  of five people who had pleaded guilty  and testified under cooperation  agreements  they included jacob kingston and his  younger brother isaiah  prosecutors showed at trial that they  made  nearly 500 million dollars and that the  claims accelerated  at the end of the fraud he then  sent through a very complex financial  path  tens of millions of dollars to left  german  [Music]  now to an eyewitness news investigation  and the strange alliance between a  suspected mobster here in l.a  and a polygamous clan in utah lev durman  was  convicted in march of 2020  after a six-week trial of conspiracy  money laundering and fraud charges  german's lawyer complained  that the jurors panicked and reached  a quick decision only because they were  scared about covet 19 and they wanted to  get out of there  i've known my client for decades and i'm  i'm confident that when he tells me he  did nothing wrong that he's telling the  truth  the second phase of lev durman's  criminal trial  will be a forfeiture proceeding that  begins later this year  in which the government is trying to  recover assets that they say were the  product of money laundering  both lev durman and jacob kingston are  in jail around salt lake city  neither has been sentenced lev durman  faces life in prison jacob kingston  also faces many years in prison but as a  result of his cooperation  and the successful conviction of leb  durman  it's likely that he would get far less  time than he  ultimately could face for the crimes he  admitted in pleading guilty  the kingston fraud was the largest  biodiesel fuel fraud in u.s history  more than 30 cases no one had been  accused  the level of fraud that they engaged in  that they admitted engaging in  you

